  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1047 PM CDT TUE OCT 20 2026\n\nDry northwesterly to northerly flow aloft persists through\nThursday, between ridging over the Southern Plains and troughing\nalong the East Coast. At the surface, high pressure over the\neastern CONUS maintains a dry continental air mass, while a\nsurface low moves slowly northeastward off of the Mid-Atlantic/Northeast\ncoastlines. Cool nights and temperatures near to slightly above \naverage are expected with no rain. Friday through the weekend the\nlow pressure system over the western Atlantic exits, while a \ncutoff low forms near Cuba. This allows the mid-level subtropical \nridge to build eastward, but a strengthening CAD wedge in the wake\nof the Atlantic system results in slightly cooler high \ntemperatures for the weekend. A shortwave trough approaches the \narea next week, but little to no moisture return is indicated at \nthis time as high pressure persists at the surface.\n\n32/JDavis",
